## 1️⃣ Trending attractions in Prague’s Old Town (the “centre”)

| # | Attraction | Why it’s trending in 2024 | Practical visitor info |
|---|------------|---------------------------|------------------------|
| **1** | **Charles Bridge (Karlův most)** | • Night‑time illumination and occasional live‑classical concerts make it a top Instagram spot.<br>• The bridge’s “Bridge Tower” (Old Town Bridge Tower) was recently restored, drawing extra foot‑traffic. | • **Open 24 h – free** to walk.<br>• Best time: **6‑8 am** (few crowds) or **after sunset** for magical lighting.<br>• Nearby: **Old Town Bridge Tower** ticket €5 (skip‑the‑line online). |
| **2** | **Old Town Square & Astronomical Clock (Staroměstské náměstí)** | • The festive **Christmas market** (Nov – Dec) is one of the most‑visited in Europe.<br>• The hourly “clock show” (except 5‑6 am) still amazes tourists. | • **Free** to roam the square.<br>• Clock show: every hour.<br>• **Old Town Hall Tower** ticket €10 (online tickets avoid queues). |
| **3** | **Prague Castle (Pražský hrad) – St. Vitus Cathedral & Golden Lane** | • Restoration of St. Vit’s stained‑glass windows (completed early 2024) has boosted visitor interest.<br>• The castle complex remains the **most‑visited historic site** in the Czech Republic. | • Opening: **9 am – 5 pm** (last entry 4:30 pm).<br>• Combined ticket (castle grounds, St. Vitus, Golden Lane, etc.) €15.<br>• English guided tour (45 min) €8 – book in advance. |
| **4** | **Jewish Quarter (Josefov) – Old‑New Synagogue & Jewish Museum** | • UNESCO‑listed heritage; the museum’s refreshed **Holocaust Remembrance exhibition** launched Jan 2024.<br>• The Old‑New Synagogue’s “Golem” legend continues to attract curious visitors. | • Combined ticket (all sites) €20.<br>• Audio guide (multiple languages) €5.<br>• Open **9 am – 6 pm** (closed Saturdays). |
| **5** | **Petrin Hill & Observation Tower** | • The “mini‑Eiffel” tower offers panoramic city views; the hill’s **rose garden** is especially fragrant in early December.<br>• Funicular ride (€3 round‑trip) makes it accessible for families. | • Tower opening: **9 am – 5 pm** (last entry 4:30 pm).<br>• Entrance (incl. funicular) €8.<br>• Sunset (≈ 4 pm) gives the best photo light. |
| **6** | **National Theatre (Národní divadlo)** | • New productions of **“The Magic Flute”** (opera) and **“Hamlet”** (theatre) have sold out quickly – a cultural highlight for visitors. | • Guided backstage tour €12.<br>• Show tickets start at €25 (book early).<br>• Located on the Vltava riverbank, perfect for an evening stroll. |

> **All of these attractions are within a 10‑minute walk of each other** in the Old Town (Staré Město) and across the Vltava River, so you’ll spend almost no time commuting.

