## 3️⃣ Suggested 7‑day itinerary (flexible)

| Day | Morning | Mid‑day | Evening |
|-----|---------|---------|----------|
| **Day 1 – 10 Dec** | Arrive, check‑in, settle in | Walk to **Old Town Square**, watch the Astronomical Clock show, explore surrounding lanes | Dinner at **Mlejnice** (traditional Czech) – 5‑min walk |
| **Day 2** | **Charles Bridge** sunrise walk, climb Old Town Bridge Tower | Lunch at **Café Savoy** (classic Viennese‑style) | Evening Vltava river cruise (≈ €25) |
| **Day 3** | **Prague Castle** – guided tour (St. Vitus, Golden Lane) | Lunch at **U Kříže** (castle district) | Night‑time stroll across Charles Bridge, enjoy street‑music |
| **Day 4** | **Jewish Quarter** – Old‑New Synagogue, Jewish Museum | Lunch at **Maitrea** (vegetarian, near the square) | Attend a performance at the **National Theatre** (book tickets early) |
| **Day 5** | **Petrin Hill** – funicular, Observation Tower, Rose Garden | Picnic on the hill (grab pastries from **Café Lípa**) | Return to Old Town, cocktail at **Hotel Paris Prague rooftop** |
| **Day 6** | Free day – optional day‑trip to **Kutná Hora** (Bone Church) or **Karlovy Vary** (spa town) – both 2‑hour train rides | Return late afternoon | Dinner at **Lokál Dlouhááá** (authentic Czech beer hall) |
| **Day 7 – 17 Dec** | Last‑minute souvenir shopping (Mánes Bridge market) | Check‑out, airport shuttle (≈ €6 per person) | Fly home |

*All times are approximate; you can shift activities to match your pace.*

